WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.960
- Welcome back, everyone
for our discussion session

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.790
following Professor Alex
Paseau's talk yesterday.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.970
And I am delighted to
introduce our conversant

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.240
for this afternoon, Professor Gila Sher

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.570
of the University of
California at San Diego.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.580
We are delighted to have you here

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.103
and Alex we are delighted
to have you back.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.110
And as a philosophy professor
her research interests

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:38.280
have focused on the foundational
issues in epistemology,

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.850
the philosophy of logic
and the theory of truth.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.890
Her books include "The Bounds of Logic:

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.297
A Generalized Viewpoint" from MIT Press,

00:00:46.297 --> 00:00:49.500
"Epistemic Friction: An Essay
on Knowledge, Truth and Logic"

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.160
from Oxford University Press
and "Logical Consequence"

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.320
from the Cambridge University Press.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.987
She's currently working on
a book provisionally titled,

00:00:58.987 --> 00:01:02.520
"Truth as a Human Value,"
which sounds fascinating,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.280
which offers a reconception
of the philosophy of truth

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.740
in light of the post-truth crisis.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.930
So without further ado,

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.790
let me invite Professor
Gila Sher to take the floor.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:15.623
- Thank you.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.180
Okay, I would like first to
thank Priya for inviting me

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.540
to be a discussant and
I'd like to thank Alex

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.800
for an extremely
interesting talk yesterday.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.610
I also listened to some of
the talks on your webpage

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.593
and they're really fascinating.

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:38.700
So I started by short introduction,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.420
There's Much More to
Logic Than Recognized,

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.273
and this is a citation from Alex.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.467
Now, I agree with most of
the things that Alex says

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.453
about true, sorry, about logic.

00:01:55.456 --> 00:01:59.460
There is much more to logic
than commonly recognized.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.780
One of the things is
that logic is not finite

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.110
in ways it is commonly thought to be.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:11.970
In addition to a bottom-up
way of understanding logic

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:16.200
based on the way we commonly
use it in everyday discourse,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:21.200
there is also a top-down
theoretical understanding of logic

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:25.950
that shows that logic is
stronger than commonly thought.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.240
A very important theoretical
consideration of this kind

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.753
is the strong degree
of invariance of logic

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.820
that Alex talked about.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.550
This has to do with the topic neutrality

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:42.570
and other special features
of logic such as formality,

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:45.390
necessity, and generality.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.570
But there are also significant relations

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:52.530
between purely logical
or deductive inferences

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.250
and non-logical, non-deductive inferences.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:01.250
Not all good inferences, I
agree with Alex, are logical.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.683
Since I agree with Alex,
I won't criticize him,

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.140
but I approach logic

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.980
from a somewhat different
perspective than him.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:17.220
So I will try to broaden the perspective,

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.020
hence the significance of
what Alex said about logic

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:26.340
and I will ask him if he
agrees with this broadening.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.710
Among other things I will address

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:33.000
the question of truth in
logic and I will try to give

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.330
a tentative answer to two of the questions

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.420
that Priya asked Alex yesterday,

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:42.660
what is special to the
structure of mathematics

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.347
compared to physics and why?

00:03:46.347 --> 00:03:49.320
And I would add whether mathematics

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.460
can't be affected by experimentation?

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.740
Let's start with truth.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:59.460
Alex gave a simple example
of a logical inference

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.453
or implication, I will use
them interchangeably here.

00:04:04.342 --> 00:04:08.310
If the inference is if
A, then B: if B, then C:

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.310
therefore, if A, then C, and
here it is in symbols too.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:18.950
Now, is it true that this is
a logically valid inference?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.690
Or take this inference,

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.690
for some X, PX or QX, for all X, not PX,

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.833
therefore for some X, QX.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:36.783
Is it true that this
inference is logically valid?

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:43.170
Now, the above inferences
seem to be logically valid,

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:46.060
but is it true that
they are logically valid

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.710
and if it is, why?

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:54.710
And does this answer extend
to infinitary inferences

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.903
like the ones that Alex talked about?

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:02.220
Some people say that there is no truth

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.410
and falsehood in logic.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:08.670
Logic is just a game and like all games

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:11.370
the logical game has its rules

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:15.060
which tell us when we
win and when we lose,

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.450
but this has nothing to do with truth.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.990
For example, the late Wittgenstein said

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.780
that logic is a language game.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:29.490
Carnap said that logic
is merely conventional.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:32.430
There is no right and wrong in logic.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:36.660
There is only what we like
or what is convenient.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.930
This leads to a pragmatist, relativist

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.273
and pluralist views of logic.

00:05:43.191 --> 00:05:46.830
Alex, I should note, is an anti-pluralist,

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.170
he is a monist about logic.

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:52.287
His book is titled "The One True Logic."

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.470
Now, even if you believe

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:58.650
that there is truth and falsehood in logic

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.030
and that it's true

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.780
that the above inferences
are logically valid,

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:08.160
the question arises why
or in virtue of what?

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.260
Is it true that there are logically valid?

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:16.230
Some philosophers, perhaps
most philosophers say

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:19.050
that this is a matter of language.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:20.763
Logical inferences are analytic.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:25.653
English users treat
them as logically valid.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.940
When we put these two approaches together,

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:33.360
we arrive at the view
that logical inferences

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.740
are just winning moves in a language game.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.730
And this was Wittgeinstein's view.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:46.730
What I wanna show is that
logic is neither a game

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:50.670
nor grounded merely in language.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:55.670
I will do this first in a
bottom-top way by an example.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:01.020
Claim, logic is not just a language game.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.980
Logic must be constrained by the world.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.500
Truth in the world can be a matter

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.050
of life and death in logic,

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:13.200
not just winning or losing a game.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.260
And being constrained
by the world makes logic

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.173
similar to physics and other sciences.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:23.523
Here is a short story
that demonstrates this.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:29.070
Abe is a young naive
student at University X.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:32.700
He takes seriously
everything his professors,

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:37.680
especially his more extravagant
professors teach him.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:42.680
One day a new logic professor
joins Abe's university,

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:47.840
and he's eccentric, extravagant
and exciting as Abe likes.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.330
The new professor tells students

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.630
that logic is nothing more than a game.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:58.200
He shares with them one
of his favorite rules

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.000
which belongs to a new,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.510
non-traditional logic game he invented.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:07.774
He calls this rule modus davka.

00:08:07.774 --> 00:08:12.210
Now, davka is a Hebrew
word which means willfully,

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:15.930
spitefully, deliberately
doing the opposite

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.690
of what you are expected to do.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:22.383
And the rule modus davka is the following,

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:26.790
first we have a premise if A, then not B,

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:30.963
then we have the premise
A, and we conclude B.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:35.490
Abe is excited about modus davka.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:38.553
He decides to follow it
in his everyday life.

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:44.130
Modus davka is not a
traditional rule of inference.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:47.280
It's superficially similar to an instance

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.420
of a traditional logical
rule, modus ponens

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:54.210
which the instance would say

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:59.190
if A, then not B, A, therefore not B.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:00.903
But it's different.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:06.930
Standing on the side of a
busy road in town one day,

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.810
Abe is getting ready to cross it.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:13.200
His parents told him if a car is coming

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.970
don't cross the road,
Abe takes one to be true.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:22.590
It is the conditional command
analog of a true sentence,

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.110
hence essentially true.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:27.720
Abe checks whether a car is coming

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:32.400
and sees that one is
coming, indeed many are.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.580
Remembering his new exciting teacher's

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:36.933
favorite logical rule,

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:42.920
MD: If A, then not B; A therefore: B,

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.533
Abe crosses the road, Abe dies.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.090
MD may be an exciting rule

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.540
but it does not work in the world.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.680
In contrast rules that
are grounded in the world

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.470
like modus ponens do.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:05.490
Modus ponens is grounded in the world.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:10.490
It says if A then not
B, A therefore not B.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.580
Had Abe followed MP instead of MD,

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.320
he would not have crossed the road

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.050
and would not have been killed by a car,

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.643
at least at that time.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:25.920
Now, this was a bottom-up
argument for the claim

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.623
that logic is constrained by the world,

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.740
but can we establish it also

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:35.490
using a top-down theoretical argument?

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:38.790
Can we establish this by an argument about

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:42.690
the nature of logic of
the kind used by Alex

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:46.533
to establish the infinitary
cocktail of logic?

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:51.930
I think we can, but first
I would like address

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:55.980
the methodological issue
of providing a top-down

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.100
theoretical foundation for logic.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:03.180
Is it possible to provide
a foundation for logic?

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.050
Many philosophers believe
that it's impossible.

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:10.290
To provide a foundation for X, they say,

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:15.290
you have to go outside X, but
we cannot go outside logic,

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:20.340
we cannot make any step in
thought without using logic.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:24.240
A foundation for logic will be circular.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:27.600
This was the view of
the young Wittgenstein

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.980
and many past and present
philosophers share.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.813
I don't, why?

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:39.860
The methodology used in
foundational studies in philosophy,

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:44.693
the traditional one is foundationalism.

00:11:44.693 --> 00:11:48.690
It says that in order to provide
a foundation for knowledge,

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.870
all units of knowledge have to be grounded

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:54.390
in something which is lower than them

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:57.770
in the foundational
hierarchy until in the end

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:01.020
they're all grounded in the base.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:04.470
The problem is that there is
nothing lower than the base.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:08.700
So it is in principle
impossible to ground the base.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.130
Since everything depends on the base,

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.770
nothing can be grounded.

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:16.320
In the case of logic, it's more direct

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:19.980
because everyone puts logic in the base.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.670
What I believe is that
there is more than one

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:28.170
foundational methodology and
a more fruitful methodology

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:31.200
is what I call foundational wholism,

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.900
here we have our system of knowledge.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.360
Different branches and different parts

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:41.130
are connected to the world in
different ways in many places

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:45.180
and they are all connected
also among themselves.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:48.720
In order to arrive at knowledge

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.670
or to give a foundation for knowledge,

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:53.460
we have to ground it on
the one hand in the world

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.020
through these all connections
and we can also help ourselves

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:01.680
by utilizing the connections,
the internal connections

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.110
between fields of knowledge.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:06.240
The process is dynamic

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.230
and it goes in a back and forth manner.

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:14.850
Once we have a tentative
foundation for something,

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:18.480
we move to another part of
our system of knowledge,

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:23.480
use new resources that
we got in the meantime

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:28.850
and we examine our original foundation.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:31.521
Whenever there is secularity,

00:13:31.521 --> 00:13:34.500
it is usually temporary and partial.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:38.580
It is partial because we
always use many sources

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.130
in order to find something.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.340
For example, in the case of
logic, we use philosophy,

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:47.250
mathematics, general
knowledge, common sense,

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:51.990
besides using logic and
it's all also temporary

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:56.850
because we always come back
and reexamine our foundation

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:00.750
and assume different things and put aside

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.213
things we assume in the past.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:08.160
So using the foundational
holistic methodology,

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:11.310
one way to go about providing a foundation

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.620
for logic is this,

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:17.340
we start observations about knowledge,

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:22.340
one, for one reason or another
human beings are interested

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.590
in knowing the world as it is,

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:30.590
but, two, such knowledge does
not come to them automatically

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:35.133
and in many cases it is
quite difficult to arrive at.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.150
This is largely due to the limitations

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.970
of our cognitive resources.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:44.940
One result of these limitations

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.880
is that we are prone to error.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.900
This is where truth
enters into the picture.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:56.580
We need truth, we need a
norm or a standard of truth

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.993
to avoid error.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:02.820
Another result is that we need shortcuts.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:07.680
We cannot discover each facet
of the world individually.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:11.910
This is where methods of
inference come into play.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:16.530
We would especially benefit
from having a genuine method

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:20.250
for arriving from truth
that we already know

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.490
to truth that we don't yet know.

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:27.393
The function of logic is
to provide such a method.

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:32.700
Now, because our goal is
true theories of the world,

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:37.700
it's very important that logical
influence transmits truth,

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.970
truth in the world from
premises to conclusion.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:46.650
And it's also very
desirable that logic provide

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:50.040
a strong method of transmitting truth,

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:54.000
one that works in all
almost fields of knowledge

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:58.080
and even for cases we
have not encountered yet

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.600
but might encounter in the future

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.720
that is counterfactual cases.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:08.130
So the task of logic is to
provide a method of inference

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:12.210
that transmits truth from
premises to conclusion

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:16.620
with a considerable modal
force and generality.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:21.620
A logically implies B, if
only if A transmits truth

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.453
to be necessarily and in all fields.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.333
But is this possible?

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.940
I think it is.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:34.940
And I reason as follows,
if one, in the world,

00:16:36.443 --> 00:16:41.443
if one, the world has certain
features that occur everywhere

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.890
including all parts of the world

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:46.860
that the different
fields of knowledge study

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.640
and including counterfactual situations.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:55.350
And if two, these features
are governed by laws

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:59.880
which are both highly
general and highly necessary,

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:04.320
then we could use our
knowledge of these laws

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:08.520
to create a general and
necessary method of inference,

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:12.810
a method for transmitting
truth from sentences

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:16.230
that are true in the
world to other sentences

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.120
that are true in the world.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:23.120
Expanding our knowledge to
the latter in one fell swoop.

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:27.000
This is what we are looking for,

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:32.000
features or properties F1,
F2 in the world such that

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.882
looking from the bottom-up,

00:17:34.882 --> 00:17:37.882
it is a law that F1 necessitates F2.

00:17:38.843 --> 00:17:42.343
So in the world a situation C1 that has F1

00:17:44.182 --> 00:17:47.349
necessitates situation C2 that has F2,

00:17:48.622 --> 00:17:52.455
and if S1 is true, just
in case C1 is the case

00:17:53.927 --> 00:17:56.910
and S2 is true just in
case C2 is the case,

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:01.683
then the necessation and
the level of the world

00:18:01.683 --> 00:18:06.683
ensures that the truth
of S1 strongly guarantees

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:11.340
the truth of S2, and this is
a basis for the inference,

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:15.213
S1 logically implies S2.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:20.673
Now, are there such
properties like F1 and F2?

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:26.280
Yes, formal properties are of this kind.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:30.330
Properties like identity,
complementation, union,

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:34.050
intersection, cardinality
properties such as

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:38.553
at least one having finite
cardinality and et cetera.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.960
Note that at least one
is the same property

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:44.940
as non-emptiness,

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:49.940
which is the existential
quantifier of property,

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:55.200
to say that there is at least
one P is the same as saying

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.930
P is not empty, which
is the same as saying

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:03.120
there is an X such that PX.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:06.930
Now, all the standard logical
constants and the properties

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:10.890
they denote are intuitively formal,

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:15.890
and this explains how
and why standard logical

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:18.810
content implications work.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:23.810
For example, take the
implication for some X, AX or BX

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:29.720
for all X not BX,
therefore for some X, AX.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:35.280
The premises transmit truth
necessarily to the conclusion

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.597
because in the world
there has a formal law

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:44.570
which says that the
non-emptiness of any union

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:49.580
of any properties P1 and P2
plus the emptiness of P2,

00:19:50.887 --> 00:19:55.887
here B is empty, necessitates
the non-emptiness of P1.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:02.240
This explains why the above
inference transmits truth

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:06.660
from premises to conclusion
and does so in all field

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:09.420
and with strong necessity.

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:13.230
All field, for example, in a
case of the natural numbers

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.740
A and B can be positive and negative,

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:20.010
properties of being positive and negative,

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:24.090
there is at least one number
which is positive or negative.

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:27.150
No natural number is negative,

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:30.780
therefore at least one is positive.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:34.680
And in the field of say
American presidents,

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:38.580
these could be the properties
of being a man and a woman.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:41.790
So there is at least
one American president,

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:44.010
which is a man or a woman.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:48.690
So far there are no American
presidents which are women,

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:52.283
therefore there is at
least one which is a man.

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:56.580
Now, it is important to recognize that

00:20:56.580 --> 00:21:00.671
there are more formal
properties than formal laws

00:21:00.671 --> 00:21:03.100
and formal laws and more formal laws

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:09.050
than those underlined the
inferences of standard logic.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:14.330
Okay, this correlates with
the point Alex made yesterday.

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:19.430
For example, the properties
is infinite is uncountable,

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:21.753
the second level properties are formal.

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:27.770
And uncountable P necessitates
infinite P is a formal law.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:37.800
So the inference uncountable many X, PX,

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:42.800
therefore infinitely many
X, PX also transmits truth

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:48.870
from premise to conclusion
with a strong modal force,

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.553
hence it is logical valid.

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:53.550
We have done two things.

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:56.220
One, we have provided a foundation

00:21:56.220 --> 00:21:58.980
for standard logical inferences,

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:02.100
and two, we expanded standard logic

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:04.710
based on the same foundation.

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:07.320
But we also did a third thing.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:10.440
We expanded logic and inferences

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:14.430
to inferences that deal with infinities.

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:18.753
Such inferences are not
recognized by standard logic.

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:24.420
This is another aspect of the
infinitary character of logic

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:26.730
and as we should shortly see,

00:22:26.730 --> 00:22:30.660
it is equivalent to the
infinitary character

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:35.040
of Alex's infinitary
logic which has to do with

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:37.080
infinitely long conjunctions,

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:39.393
disjunctions and quantifications.

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:43.350
But in order to reach this result

00:22:43.350 --> 00:22:47.790
and in order to further systematize
our foundation of logic,

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:51.690
we need to systematically
characterize formality,

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:53.730
formal properties.

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:58.620
And this leads us to the
fascinating topic of invariance,

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:00.573
that Alex talked about.

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:05.490
Invariance is a central topic of interest

00:23:05.490 --> 00:23:08.460
in both science and mathematics.

00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:12.000
But the invariance used
in the foundation of logic

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:16.380
is a bit different, it
is property invariance,

00:23:16.380 --> 00:23:17.583
let me explain.

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:23.400
Every property whatsoever has
some degree of invariance.

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:25.500
What does this mean?

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:29.550
It means that every
property remains the same

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:34.550
under some one-to-one and onto
replacements of individuals.

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:39.060
Example, the property is a human.

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:42.840
If you replace individuals which are men

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:47.840
by individuals which are
women in a one-to-one manner,

00:23:48.180 --> 00:23:51.920
the property is a human will not notice,

00:23:51.920 --> 00:23:55.983
it is invariant under such replacement.

00:23:57.660 --> 00:24:01.650
Most properties, however,
are not invariant

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:06.650
under all one-to-one and on to
replacements of individuals.

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:12.020
For example, is a human, is
invariant under replacements

00:24:12.270 --> 00:24:16.170
of men by women but not under replacements

00:24:16.170 --> 00:24:18.480
of men by numbers.

00:24:18.480 --> 00:24:21.330
When we replaced Biden by the number one

00:24:21.330 --> 00:24:24.960
and Trump by the number two
and Obama by the number three,

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:29.160
and so on, we replace
the property, is a human,

00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:31.323
by the property is a number.

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:37.170
But some properties are
invariant under all one-to-one

00:24:37.170 --> 00:24:40.650
and onto replacements of individuals.

00:24:40.650 --> 00:24:43.800
For example, self-identity.

00:24:43.800 --> 00:24:47.070
Biden is self-identical and so is one,

00:24:47.070 --> 00:24:49.410
Trump is self-identical and so is two,

00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:52.173
and similarly Obama and three.

00:24:53.070 --> 00:24:58.070
Indeed maximally invariant
properties are invariant

00:24:59.310 --> 00:25:02.610
not just under one-to-one replacements

00:25:02.610 --> 00:25:04.890
of actual individuals,

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:08.100
but also under one-to-one replacements

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:11.040
of counterfactual individuals.

00:25:11.040 --> 00:25:15.690
For example, identity is
invariant under all one-to-one

00:25:15.690 --> 00:25:20.690
and onto replacements of actual
counterfactual individuals.

00:25:21.540 --> 00:25:25.110
If we replace Biden then
by Hamlet for example,

00:25:25.110 --> 00:25:29.430
we also replace an individual
which is identical to itself

00:25:29.430 --> 00:25:33.600
and only to itself by an
individual which is identical

00:25:33.600 --> 00:25:36.360
to itself and only to itself.

00:25:36.360 --> 00:25:40.563
Identity is not affected
by such a replacement.

00:25:41.400 --> 00:25:45.870
In fact, all the formal
properties in our examples above

00:25:45.870 --> 00:25:47.850
are of this kind.

00:25:47.850 --> 00:25:50.910
Consider is known empty,

00:25:50.910 --> 00:25:54.150
the existential quantifier property.

00:25:54.150 --> 00:25:57.720
Take any domains with the
same number of individuals,

00:25:57.720 --> 00:26:00.990
for example, D1 is Biden, Trump, Obama

00:26:00.990 --> 00:26:03.450
and D2, one, two, three.

00:26:03.450 --> 00:26:06.990
Now, replace the members
of D1 by members of D2

00:26:06.990 --> 00:26:10.980
in a one-to-one manner,
for example as above.

00:26:10.980 --> 00:26:15.270
Next take any property of objects in D1,

00:26:15.270 --> 00:26:18.930
say is a Democratic president.

00:26:18.930 --> 00:26:23.660
This property satisfies
non-emptiness in D1

00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:29.670
but also its image under
the one-to-one replacement

00:26:29.670 --> 00:26:33.720
is non-empty, its image is the property

00:26:33.720 --> 00:26:38.720
A being an odd numbers,
Biden is correlated with one

00:26:38.820 --> 00:26:43.820
and Obama with three, and these
property also is non-empty.

00:26:43.860 --> 00:26:47.910
So non-emptiness does
not notice is invariant

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:52.910
under this replacement,
and this holds generally.

00:26:52.920 --> 00:26:55.890
Let us call properties that are invariant

00:26:55.890 --> 00:26:59.340
under all one-to-one and onto replacements

00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:02.850
of actual counterfactual individuals

00:27:02.850 --> 00:27:05.643
maximally invariant properties.

00:27:06.810 --> 00:27:10.290
We seem to have two very
interesting results.

00:27:10.290 --> 00:27:14.220
One, all the standards logical properties,

00:27:14.220 --> 00:27:17.716
the properties denoted
by the logical constants

00:27:17.716 --> 00:27:19.988
are maximally invariant.

00:27:19.988 --> 00:27:24.988
Two, other properties including
infinitistic properties

00:27:25.770 --> 00:27:29.100
such as infinitely many
and accountably many

00:27:29.100 --> 00:27:32.730
are also maximally invariant.

00:27:32.730 --> 00:27:35.460
We also have results that enable us

00:27:35.460 --> 00:27:38.793
to give a precise definition of formality.

00:27:40.050 --> 00:27:43.840
A property P is maximally
invariant if and only if

00:27:43.840 --> 00:27:47.640
it is invariant under all isomorphisms.

00:27:47.640 --> 00:27:49.410
What does this mean?

00:27:49.410 --> 00:27:52.400
For example, identity is invariant

00:27:52.400 --> 00:27:55.230
and that does not distinguish between

00:27:55.230 --> 00:27:59.160
any isomorphic structures
of the form D domain

00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:01.683
and a pair of individuals A, B.

00:28:02.700 --> 00:28:07.700
A is identical to be and the
structure DAB is isomorphic

00:28:08.850 --> 00:28:13.110
to the structure D prime, A prime, B prime

00:28:13.110 --> 00:28:17.823
if and only if A prime
is identical to B prime.

00:28:18.750 --> 00:28:23.293
Now, intuitively a property
is isomorphism invariant

00:28:25.110 --> 00:28:29.160
if and only if it is highly structural.

00:28:29.160 --> 00:28:32.850
It follows from one
and two that a property

00:28:32.850 --> 00:28:35.960
is maximally invariant if and only if

00:28:35.960 --> 00:28:38.490
it is highly structural.

00:28:38.490 --> 00:28:41.940
And since to be formal is intuitively

00:28:41.940 --> 00:28:46.740
to be highly structural, we
now have a precise definition

00:28:46.740 --> 00:28:51.740
of formality, property P
is formal is by definition

00:28:52.230 --> 00:28:54.543
P is maximally invariant.

00:28:55.800 --> 00:29:00.800
Another interesting result
is if a property is formal,

00:29:00.990 --> 00:29:05.580
the laws governing it
are highly necessary.

00:29:05.580 --> 00:29:09.840
Reason, if a property does not distinguish

00:29:09.840 --> 00:29:14.430
between any actual
counterfactual individuals,

00:29:14.430 --> 00:29:18.480
its laws cannot distinguish
between them either.

00:29:18.480 --> 00:29:20.820
If they hold in any domain

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:23.430
of actual counterfactual individuals,

00:29:23.430 --> 00:29:25.680
they hold in all domains

00:29:25.680 --> 00:29:28.830
of actual counterfactual individuals,

00:29:28.830 --> 00:29:32.070
hence they are necessary.

00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:34.800
It follows, all implications

00:29:34.800 --> 00:29:38.460
based on formal laws are necessary.

00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:42.930
This explains why all the
standard logical implications

00:29:42.930 --> 00:29:45.960
as well as infinitistic implications

00:29:45.960 --> 00:29:49.890
like uncomfortably many X, PX,

00:29:49.890 --> 00:29:54.890
therefore infinitely
many X, PX are necessary.

00:29:54.930 --> 00:29:58.680
They transmit truth from
premises to conclusion

00:29:58.680 --> 00:30:01.590
with a very strong modal force,

00:30:01.590 --> 00:30:04.380
hence they satisfy the requirements

00:30:04.380 --> 00:30:09.063
and logical implications,
I.e, they are logically valid.

00:30:10.140 --> 00:30:13.290
Next we arrived at Mcgee's result

00:30:13.290 --> 00:30:16.290
that Alex relied on yesterday.

00:30:16.290 --> 00:30:20.970
A property is formal if
and only if it is definable

00:30:20.970 --> 00:30:24.690
in the logic L infinity, infinity.

00:30:24.690 --> 00:30:29.690
This means that all infinitary
implications in Alex's sense

00:30:30.390 --> 00:30:31.233
are logical.

00:30:32.370 --> 00:30:37.370
Finally, there is an interesting
concerning mathematics.

00:30:37.740 --> 00:30:41.583
All higher level mathematical
properties are formal.

00:30:42.450 --> 00:30:45.930
Now, since all mathematical individuals

00:30:45.930 --> 00:30:50.930
and their lower level mathematical
properties are correlated

00:30:51.270 --> 00:30:54.870
with higher level mathematical properties,

00:30:54.870 --> 00:30:59.310
all of mathematics is essentially formal.

00:30:59.310 --> 00:31:01.350
What do I mean by this correlation?

00:31:01.350 --> 00:31:03.600
For example, the number one

00:31:03.600 --> 00:31:06.922
which is a mathematical
individual is correlated

00:31:06.922 --> 00:31:11.922
with the second level
mathematical property exactly one

00:31:13.650 --> 00:31:18.030
as in there is exactly one moon of earth,

00:31:18.030 --> 00:31:21.993
and this is how it's
usually used in science.

00:31:22.890 --> 00:31:27.890
Let me conclude with a few
results concerning the difference

00:31:28.110 --> 00:31:33.000
and similarities between
mathematics and science.

00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:36.090
Differences between
mathematics and science,

00:31:36.090 --> 00:31:40.833
and this addresses the points
that Priya raise yesterday.

00:31:42.270 --> 00:31:47.270
The fact that mathematics is
formal maximally invariant

00:31:48.090 --> 00:31:52.620
explains what is special
about mathematics.

00:31:52.620 --> 00:31:55.920
Mathematics is maximally invariant,

00:31:55.920 --> 00:31:59.550
hence its laws are highly necessary.

00:31:59.550 --> 00:32:03.273
Physical properties are
not maximally invariant.

00:32:04.500 --> 00:32:07.500
Their laws have a weaker necessity

00:32:07.500 --> 00:32:10.530
than the logical mathematical laws.

00:32:10.530 --> 00:32:14.070
For example, physical laws
distinguish between numbers

00:32:14.070 --> 00:32:17.067
and physical objects
they hold of the latter

00:32:18.446 --> 00:32:20.430
but not of the format.

00:32:20.430 --> 00:32:25.410
Because physical concern
physical properties

00:32:25.410 --> 00:32:28.290
which are not maximally invariant,

00:32:28.290 --> 00:32:31.830
they are generally not
relevant to mathematics.

00:32:31.830 --> 00:32:35.250
They don't make a
difference to mathematics.

00:32:35.250 --> 00:32:39.213
Mathematics does not notice
that, it is blind to that.

00:32:40.419 --> 00:32:42.930
On the other hand, there
are also similarities

00:32:42.930 --> 00:32:46.560
between mathematics and
science, as Alex pointed

00:32:46.560 --> 00:32:50.460
or in the spirit of what he pointed out.

00:32:50.460 --> 00:32:54.690
A, although mathematical
properties, I'm sorry,

00:32:54.690 --> 00:32:59.690
physical properties are
not maximally invariant,

00:33:01.410 --> 00:33:06.410
some physical properties
like being subject to gravity

00:33:07.350 --> 00:33:11.460
have a fairly strong degree of invariance.

00:33:11.460 --> 00:33:14.760
They are invariant under all one-to-one

00:33:14.760 --> 00:33:18.783
and onto replacements of
physically possible individuals.

00:33:19.890 --> 00:33:22.833
Any replacement of physical individuals,

00:33:22.833 --> 00:33:26.790
will get you from individual,
which is subject to gravity

00:33:26.790 --> 00:33:29.760
to an individual which
is subject to gravity.

00:33:29.760 --> 00:33:32.130
And even in the counterfactual case,

00:33:32.130 --> 00:33:35.610
say a second moon of earth,
that will be the case,

00:33:35.610 --> 00:33:40.410
a second moon of earth
will be subject to gravity.

00:33:40.410 --> 00:33:42.960
Therefore, their laws also have

00:33:42.960 --> 00:33:45.993
a fairly strong degree of necessity.

00:33:46.950 --> 00:33:51.000
B, because physical objects and properties

00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:53.040
have formal properties,

00:33:53.040 --> 00:33:57.600
for example, the property
of being a moon of earth,

00:33:57.600 --> 00:34:00.840
the physical property
has the formal property

00:34:00.840 --> 00:34:05.700
of having cardinality one,
mathematics and logic,

00:34:05.700 --> 00:34:10.560
which are formal theories are
widely applicable to physics.

00:34:10.560 --> 00:34:12.960
They deal with formal properties

00:34:12.960 --> 00:34:17.340
which are properties of physical objects

00:34:17.340 --> 00:34:19.620
and physical properties.

00:34:19.620 --> 00:34:23.760
This gives a new answer to
Wagner's famous question

00:34:23.760 --> 00:34:28.560
about the unreasonable
effectiveness of mathematics

00:34:28.560 --> 00:34:32.673
and I would add logic
in the natural sciences.

00:34:33.840 --> 00:34:37.500
The fact that physical
objects have formal properties

00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:41.640
and are governed by
formal laws explains also

00:34:41.640 --> 00:34:46.640
how sometimes physical results
are relevant to mathematics.

00:34:46.980 --> 00:34:51.570
Whenever we get a new refutation
of a scientific conjecture,

00:34:51.570 --> 00:34:55.530
there is a possibility
that the mistake concerns

00:34:55.530 --> 00:34:58.230
formal assumptions we made

00:34:58.230 --> 00:35:01.110
concerning the physical situation.

00:35:01.110 --> 00:35:05.220
This gives us a motivation to reexamine

00:35:05.220 --> 00:35:06.990
our formal assumptions

00:35:06.990 --> 00:35:11.013
and our background mathematical
theories more generally.

00:35:12.540 --> 00:35:15.480
I will end with a question to Alex,

00:35:15.480 --> 00:35:19.260
my philosophical understanding
of logic and mathematics

00:35:19.260 --> 00:35:23.730
support and expands many of your results,

00:35:23.730 --> 00:35:26.550
but people can agree on some things

00:35:26.550 --> 00:35:31.550
yet give them different
philosophical explanations.

00:35:32.037 --> 00:35:35.940
Are these philosophical
explanations of your result

00:35:35.940 --> 00:35:40.140
in agreement with your own
general philosophical conception

00:35:40.140 --> 00:35:41.370
of logic?

00:35:41.370 --> 00:35:44.520
And if not, what is your take

00:35:44.520 --> 00:35:49.520
on the philosophical foundation
of logic, logical inference,

00:35:49.560 --> 00:35:54.560
which underlies from your
point of your results?

00:35:54.750 --> 00:35:55.583
Thank you.

00:35:56.820 --> 00:35:58.470
- Thank you so much, Gila

00:35:58.470 --> 00:36:01.680
for engaging both with Alex
and many of the questions,

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:04.230
mine and others that came up yesterday.

00:36:04.230 --> 00:36:08.170
So Alex, the floor is
